  "term": "endarterectomy",
  "definition": "Endarterectomy, in this context carotid endarterectomy, is a revascularization surgery used in people with major carotid artery atherosclerosis to lower stroke risk by helping restore the brain’s blood and oxygen supply. In cognitive research, it is also examined for possible effects on brain function and cognitive abilities after surgery.",
